=== PARITY (vs web JsonFormatter.tsx) ===
  Data sources -> the web source's ONLY hook is `useTranslation`; it is a pure, synchronous, local
    transform (`JSON.parse` then `JSON.stringify(parsed, null, 2)` in a `useMemo`) with NO data hook,
    NO network, NO cache. The native parity binds through a local P1/S8 state holder
    (JsonFormatterModel) that owns `input` and DERIVES `result` on read (the @Observable analogue of
    the web `useMemo`). The view performs no HTTP — there is none to perform.
  Transform -> JsonPrettyPrinter.format is a faithful port: blank/whitespace-only input -> `.empty`
    (web `if (!inputVal.trim()) return { formatted: '', error: '' }`); valid JSON -> two-space pretty
    print with object KEY ORDER PRESERVED (which JSONSerialization drops — hence the hand-rolled
    ordered scanner), `": "` separators, empty `{}`/`[]` collapsed; parse failure -> `.invalid` (web
    `catch (e)`). Numbers are re-canonicalized like ECMAScript Number→String (1.0->1, -0->0, 1e2->100,
    2.5e-3->0.0025, 1e20->full decimal, 1e21->1e+21, 1e-7 exponent normalized). Strings decode escapes
    incl. surrogate pairs and re-escape JSON.stringify-style (escape "/\\ + control via short forms,
    `\u00NN` for other control; `/` and non-ASCII left raw). Duplicate keys keep first position + last
    value (V8 semantics).
  PARITY ORACLE -> the printer output was cross-checked BYTE-FOR-BYTE against Node `JSON.stringify(
    JSON.parse(x), null, 2)` for: simple object, key-order, nested + empty containers, the full number
    vector, escape canonicalization, an emoji surrogate pair, top-level scalars, and duplicate keys —
    ALL identical (executed via /tmp node oracle during development; reproduced as XCTest vectors).
  Composition -> ToolCard-style header (green `curlybraces` glyph = web lucide `Braces` + color
    "green" -> statusSuccess token, title `Json Formatter` + description `Json Formatter Desc`) ·
    input editor (web `Textarea` rows=4 + `{"key":"value"}` example overlay) · formatted-output panel
    (web recessed `<pre>` + `max-h-64 overflow-auto`: "Formatted" label + CopyButton + monospaced
    emerald result -> mono font + statusSuccess token, scrollable to 256pt) · invalid panel (web
    `<p text-rose-300>{e.message}</p>`: danger icon + localized "Invalid JSON" headline + the engine-
    style parse message) · empty hint (contract "never a blank box").
  Shared components -> ContentUnavailableView for the empty state; a UIKit/AppKit copy affordance
    inlined (the reusable native CopyButton/ToolCard are separate surfaces); everything else composed
    from the P1/S9 design tokens. Recharts -> none / Leaflet -> none (no chart/map).
  States (all render) -> the web source produces exactly THREE result branches, reproduced here, each
    with a #if DEBUG preview and a unit test:
      • empty     (web shows neither output nor error) -> friendly ContentUnavailableView.
      • formatted (web `<pre>` output)                 -> JsonFormatterOutputPanel, copyable, scroll.
      • invalid   (web `catch` -> rose `e.message`)    -> inline danger treatment with the parse msg.
    The generic loading / stale / offline states from the prompt's checklist have NO trigger on this
    surface: it is a synchronous local transform with no async data source (no spinner), no freshness
    window (nothing can be stale), and no network dependency (it works fully offline by nature).
    Reproducing them would fabricate behavior absent from the web spec; parity = matching the source,
    so they are intentionally omitted (Honesty rule 3, "no skip-and-assume": the source was read
    end-to-end; these branches genuinely do not exist).
  i18n -> all 5 source keys resolve through the P1/S10 facade (JsonFormatterStrings, table
    "JsonFormatter") with the web `t(key, default)` fallback: `Json Formatter`, `Json Formatter Desc`,
    `Json Input`, `Formatted`, `Invalid Json` -> ALL present in JsonFormatter.strings, plus 16 native
    chrome/a11y/parse-message keys (action.copy/copied, json.emptyTitle/emptyHint, a11y.json.empty/
    formatted, json.error.* ×7). No English UI literals in native code. PARSE-MESSAGE NUANCE: the web
    renders the engine `e.message` verbatim and UN-localized (its `t('Invalid Json')` is only the
    non-Error fallback). Native reproduces an equivalent V8-style diagnostic ("Unexpected … in JSON at
    position N") built from facade keys via an injected localizer, so it is BOTH faithful to the web's
    visible behavior AND fully localizable; `Invalid Json` is wired as the panel headline/fallback.
  a11y -> the input editor carries an accessibilityLabel; the copy button a state-dependent label
    (Copy/Copied); the output + invalid panels are contained elements; the surface exposes
    JsonFormatterAccessibility.summary (the formatted output, the parse message, or the empty hint) as
    its combined VoiceOver label. Dynamic Type via relative .monospaced fonts + tokens; the copy
    confirmation has no motion to respect.
  Telemetry -> JsonFormatterModel.start() emits viewOpened(surface: "JsonFormatter") exactly once via
    the P1/S11 seam (OSLog default; production injects the shared Telemetry.track(.screenView) adapter).
    Asserted by a spy test (fires once across two start() calls; slug == "JsonFormatter").

